{"items":[{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-117678"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-117678","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-19T05:36:30.709000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://cna.erlef.org/cves/CVE-2026-117678.html","https://github.com/","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/117xxx/CVE-2026-117678.json","https://github.com/benoitc/erlang-idna","https://github.com/benoitc/erlang-idna/commit/7a465b630eb793556aa7ac282fb73e49251dadd2","https://github.com/benoitc/erlang-idna/commit/c8caba6653259071f7076fe49320f37402b8b81f","https://github.com/benoitc/erlang-idna/pull/44","https://github.com/benoitc/erlang-idna/pull/45","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-117678","https://osv.dev/vulnerability/EEF-CVE-2026-117678","https://repo.hex.pm/"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-117678"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-117678","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-117678"},"summary":"Inefficient Algorithmic Complexity vulnerability in benoitc idna allows an attacker who controls a hostname passed to the library to exhaust CPU via an over-long xn-- label. idna:ulabel/1 in src/idna.erl hands every ASCII label that starts with xn-- to punycode:decode/1 without applying check_label_length/1, the 63-octet DNS label limit. punycode:decode/1 in src/punycode.erl builds its output with list appends in insert/4, so its cost grows super-linearly with the label length. A label of a few kilobytes keeps a scheduler busy for seconds to minutes before the label is rejected as invalid punycode.\n\nEvery decode entry point reaches this path: decode/1, decode/2, to_unicode/1 and from_ascii/1. The encode path reaches it as well, because alabel/1 calls ulabel/1 on an ASCII xn-- label before its own length check, so encode/1, encode/2 and to_ascii/1 are affected for such input.\n\nThis issue affects idna: from 0.5.0 before 8.0.0.","threat_meta":null,"title":"idna: punycode labels are decoded before the 63-octet length check, so a long xn-- label causes super-linear CPU use","topics":["advisory","cwe-407"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T07:02:21.392897Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-130888"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-130888","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-19T04:55:43.967000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://access.redhat.com/downloads/content/package-browser/","https://bodhi.fedoraproject.org/updates/?packages=nbdkit","https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2575655","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/130xxx/CVE-2026-130888.json","https://gitlab.com/nbdkit/nbdkit","https://gitlab.com/nbdkit/nbdkit/-/commit/c84da7612cff7a56d842ccfe96b2a9e19bf8fea4","https://lists.libguestfs.org/archives/list/guestfs@lists.libguestfs.org/thread/LXZQCFZQQVSA2G47FMNQ3KJBMJBUVYJP/","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-130888"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-130888"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-130888","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-130888"},"summary":"A flaw was found in nbdkit. The qcow2dec filter's zstd_compressed_cluster() function incorrectly sets the ZSTD input buffer size to the uncompressed cluster size instead of the compressed buffer size. A crafted QCOW2 image with ZSTD-compressed clusters can trigger a heap over-read, leading to a denial of service and potentially exposing heap memory.","threat_meta":null,"title":"nbdkit: qcow2dec ZSTD heap over-read via incorrect input buffer size","topics":["advisory","cwe-125"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T06:00:10.326460Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-69155"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-69155","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T21:03:07.553000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/ontola/atomic-server/releases/tag/v0.40.3","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/69xxx/CVE-2026-69155.json","https://github.com/ontola/atomic-server/security/advisories/GHSA-x277-3wcg-g9r2","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-69155","https://github.com/ontola/atomic-server/commit/457c1dc9af4cd00d2aec89720718e504a49f392d","https://github.com/ontola/atomic-server/commit/8a8badfd3099765e62ccf6f92dc78a408a11106f"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-69155"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-69155","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-69155"},"summary":"Atomic Server is an open source headless CMS and real-time database. From 0.30.0 until 0.40.3, an authenticated Agent with folder write access can use POST /upload to store HTML or SVG content that GET /download/{path} serves from the application origin through server/src/handlers/download.rs. The response sets Content-Disposition: inline and lacks forced attachment handling and X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, allowing the browser to render the uploaded active content as the application. When a victim opens the link, the script can access the JavaScript-readable atomic_session cookie and the Agent private key in same-origin IndexedDB, enabling persistent account impersonation. This issue is fixed in version 0.40.3.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Atomic Server: Stored XSS via uploaded files served inline (same-origin) on `/download` → account takeover","topics":["advisory","cwe-79"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T05:45:31.739328Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-65963"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-65963","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T20:51:24.127000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/pi-hole/FTL/releases/tag/v6.7","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/65xxx/CVE-2026-65963.json","https://github.com/pi-hole/FTL/security/advisories/GHSA-8j7w-m3cr-6q6x","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-65963","https://github.com/pi-hole/FTL/commit/eb6ca080666788e16cd9405fd5899536d66c4947","https://github.com/pi-hole/FTL/pull/2935","https://github.com/pi-hole/FTL/pull/2936"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-65963"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-65963","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-65963"},"summary":"Pi-hole FTL is the core engine of the Pi-hole network-level advertisement and tracker blocker. From 6.6.2 until 6.7, PATCH /api/config accepts unfiltered CivetWeb lua_* options through webserver.advancedOpts, while POST /api/teleporter writes attacker-controlled content from a dhcp.leases archive entry through src/zip/teleporter.c without content validation. An authenticated administrator can place controlled file content on disk, point a Lua execution option at that file, and rely on the advancedOpts configuration change to restart FTL. CivetWeb then executes the file as Lua through the processing in src/webserver/webserver.c, allowing arbitrary commands to run as the pihole operating-system user and persist across restarts while the configuration and file remain. This issue is fixed in version 6.7.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Pi-hole FTL: Remote Code Execution (RCE) via CivetWeb Configuration Injection","topics":["advisory","cwe-15","cwe-20"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T06:00:10.307781Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-68918"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-68918","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T20:40:52.477000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/ikaros-dev/ikaros/releases/tag/v1.2.0","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/68xxx/CVE-2026-68918.json","https://github.com/ikaros-dev/ikaros/security/advisories/GHSA-rmp3-fcgr-5m83","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-68918","https://github.com/ikaros-dev/ikaros/commit/875ebdfbacb8bd604996b269511b0d1fe006a99b","https://github.com/ikaros-dev/ikaros/pull/852"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-68918"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-68918","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-68918"},"summary":"Ikaros is a content management system for ACGMN media. Prior to 1.2.0, server/src/main/java/run/ikaros/server/core/tag/TagEndpoint.java does not enforce tag ownership for authenticated users with tag permissions. GET /tags/condition accepts an arbitrary userId and can enumerate another user's tags, DELETE /tag/id/{id} deletes a tag without comparing its owner to the requester, and DELETE /tag/condition omits userId from its filter and can delete every user's tags matching the supplied condition. This issue is fixed in version 1.2.0.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Ikaros: Tag API Lacks Ownership Verification","topics":["advisory","cwe-639"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T06:00:10.550477Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-82038"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-82038","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T19:48:03.282000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/82xxx/CVE-2026-82038.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-82038","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bludit-through-3.22.0-improper-session-invalidation-after-user-role-demotion","https://github.com/bludit/bludit/commit/a89e2502b462c217e900f63bf2d4a2ab4edfa8e3","https://github.com/bludit/bludit/commit/f1628dd4c52a3368b39d6df678d65d4d6fc77bae","https://github.com/bludit/bludit/pull/1815","https://github.com/bludit/bludit","https://github.com/bludit/bludit/blob/3.22.0/bl-kernel/login.class.php"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-82038"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-82038","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-82038"},"summary":"Bludit through 3.22.0 contains an improper session invalidation vulnerability that allows demoted users to retain revoked privileges because Login::isLogged() never re-reads the session-stored role. Attackers holding a session issued while their account was an administrator can keep using it after demotion to perform administrator actions such as creating new administrator accounts.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Bludit through 3.22.0 Improper Session Invalidation After User Role Demotion","topics":["advisory","cwe-613"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T05:45:53.992873Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-130796"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-130796","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T19:47:59.407000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://flowiseai.com/sunset","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/130xxx/CVE-2026-130796.json","https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise/blob/main/SECURITY.md","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-130796","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/flowise-3.1.3-through-3.1.4-mcp-server-token-disclosure-via-public-chatflow-endpoint","https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise","https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise/blob/a65f81bb43ef66d3ce734bf0dff4223ae8041c95/packages/server/src/controllers/chatflows/index.ts#L229-L256","https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise/blob/a65f81bb43ef66d3ce734bf0dff4223ae8041c95/packages/server/src/database/entities/ChatFlow.ts#L64-L68","https://github.com/FlowiseAI/Flowise/blob/a65f81bb43ef66d3ce734bf0dff4223ae8041c95/packages/server/src/services/mcp-server/index.ts#L223-L250","https://github.com/geo-chen/oss/blob/main/Flowise.md"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":[],"patch_status":"unknown","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-130796","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-130796"},"summary":"Flowise 3.1.3 through 3.1.4 contains an information disclosure vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to read MCP server bearer tokens via the GET /api/v1/public-chatflows/:id handler. Attackers can use the leaked mcpServerConfig token on the POST /api/v1/mcp/:chatflowId route to invoke chatflows, bypassing API key protection and consuming the owner's model quota.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Flowise 3.1.3 through 3.1.4 MCP Server Token Disclosure via Public Chatflow Endpoint","topics":["advisory","cwe-212"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T05:45:31.917012Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-130833"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-130833","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T19:47:53.850000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/130xxx/CVE-2026-130833.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-130833","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phoboslab-pl-mpeg-through-commit-c871f2b-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-plm-demux-seek","https://github.com/phoboslab/pl_mpeg/issues/80","https://github.com/phoboslab/pl_mpeg","https://github.com/phoboslab/pl_mpeg/blob/c871f2be022ece7ef4f64230b4fb8e1fb9eb6023/pl_mpeg.h"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":[],"patch_status":"unknown","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-130833","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-130833"},"summary":"Phoboslab pl_mpeg through commit c871f2b contains an integer underflow in plm_demux_seek() that allows attackers to trigger heap out-of-bounds reads via crafted MPEG-PS files. Attackers can supply a PES packet with payload under 6 bytes, wrapping the packet->length - 6 loop bound during force_intra seeking to crash applications.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Phoboslab pl_mpeg through commit c871f2b Heap Out-of-Bounds Read via plm_demux_seek","topics":["advisory","cwe-191"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T05:45:49.339173Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-130841"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-130841","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T19:47:48.102000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/130xxx/CVE-2026-130841.json","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-130841","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/iobroker-lovelace-before-7.0.0-unauthenticated-path-traversal-via-cards-route","https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.lovelace/commit/e8dee3d08bddef088901326dab1ac7f12c2237d6","https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.lovelace","https://github.com/ioBroker/ioBroker.lovelace/blob/v6.1.3/src/lib/server.ts#L1997-L2010"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-130841"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-130841","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-130841"},"summary":"ioBroker.lovelace before 7.0.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the onCards() request handler that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to read arbitrary files via unsanitized dot-dot segments. Attackers can send crafted requests to the /cards/_static_/, /hacsfiles/, or /local/custom_ui/ routes to read files including ioBroker configuration and stored credentials.","threat_meta":null,"title":"ioBroker.lovelace before 7.0.0 Unauthenticated Path Traversal via cards Route","topics":["advisory","cwe-22"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T05:45:36.727196Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-129448"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-129448","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-17T11:03:49.685000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-82384","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/129xxx/CVE-2026-129448.json","https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/lnz4s26tv6hdo03wngtdbpfj4hg4gtds","https://lists.apache.org/thread/cc0jck13nb9vvcmzxzwotr6n16mx28z9","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-129448","https://github.com/apache/roller/pull/171","https://gitbox.apache.org/repos/asf/roller.git"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-129448"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-129448","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-129448"},"summary":"Deserialization of Untrusted Data in Apache Roller versions 4.0.0 through 6.1.4 allows an unauthenticated remote attacker to execute arbitrary code. The XML-RPC endpoint accepts vendor extension types and deserializes them before authenticating the requester.\n\nThis is the same vulnerability as CVE-2026-82384, which listed only Apache Roller 6.1.5 as affected. This issue is being actively exploited.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to Apache Roller 6.1.6 or later, which disables the extension types and rejects XML-RPC requests when the XML-RPC feature is disabled.\n\nUsers who cannot upgrade right away should set \"enabledForExtensions\" to \"false\" in WEB-INF/web.xml, or remove the \"/roller-services/xmlrpc\" servlet mapping, and restart Roller. Disabling XML-RPC in the administration UI is not enough, because older versions deserialize the request before checking that setting.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Apache Roller: Unauthenticated deserialization in the XML-RPC endpoint (releases before 6.1.5)","topics":["advisory","cwe-502"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T05:45:38.406761Z","vendors":[]},{"abstract_source":null,"affected_versions":[],"affiliations":[],"authors":[],"cves":["CVE-2026-90436"],"date_precision":"exact","fetched_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","first_seen_at":"2026-11-19T07:13:41.113156Z","id":"osv:CVE-2026-90436","is_backfill":false,"lang":"en","products":[],"published_at":"2026-11-06T15:37:55.374000Z","published_year":null,"raw_text":null,"references":["http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2026/11/06/12","https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2","https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog?field_cve=CVE-2026-90436","https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/90xxx/CVE-2026-90436.json","https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/8slf0j9gz35z56t0glt5h0ncwlbn4bdz","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-90436","https://github.com/apache/axis-axis1-java/commit/41f3b4e8d04e310ca81f86b92630ab2c11d608bd","https://gitbox.apache.org/repos/asf/axis-axis1-java.git"],"risk":{"cvss_score":null,"cvss_vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","due_date":null,"epss_percentile":null,"epss_score":null,"exploit_in_the_wild":null,"exploit_maturity":"unreported","exploit_references":[],"has_public_exploit":false,"kev_date_added":null,"kev_listed":false,"kev_status":"unknown","known_exploited":null,"known_ransomware":null,"patch_references":["https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-90436"],"patch_status":"available","severity":null},"source_info":{"link_kind":"article","native_id":"CVE-2026-90436","source":"osv","source_name":"OSV.dev","source_quality":"primary","source_sub":"osv.dev","source_url":"https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2026-90436"},"summary":"** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** Deserialization of an inbound SOAP fault in Apache Axis 1.x allows unauthenticated remote class instantiation. When a SOAP <Fault> carries a <detail><exceptionName> element, Axis loads the named class and, if a String <data> element is also present, instantiates it through its String constructor before checking that it is an AxisFault. Loading alone runs the class's static initializer. With a suitable class on the application's classpath this leads to remote code execution. The fault is parsed while the engine resolves the target service, before any per-service handler chain runs, so authentication handlers configured on a service do not protect against it. This affects all Apache Axis 1.x versions through 1.4.\n\n\n\nAs Axis 1 has been EOL we recommend you migrate to a different SOAP engine, such as Apache Axis 2/Java. Alternatively you could use a build of Axis with the patch from https://github.com/apache/axis-axis1-java/commit/41f3b4e8d04e310ca81f86b92630ab2c11d608bd applied. The Apache Axis project does not expect to create an Axis 1.x release fixing this problem.","threat_meta":null,"title":"Apache Axis 1.x (EOL): unauthenticated remote class instantiation via SOAP fault exceptionName","topics":["advisory","cwe-470"],"type":"advisory","updated_at":"2026-11-19T06:00:12.187364Z","vendors":[]}],"meta":{"cve_inputs":["CVE-2026-129446","CVE-2026-123633","CVE-2026-123007","CVE-2026-121852","CVE-2026-117678","CVE-2026-109555","CVE-2026-108687","CVE-2026-95789","CVE-2026-95787","CVE-2026-91618","CVE-2026-91585","CVE-2026-91583","CVE-2026-91570","CVE-2026-91569","CVE-2026-91510","CVE-2026-91500","CVE-2026-91470","CVE-2026-91456","CVE-2026-90817","CVE-2026-90436","CVE-2026-88711","CVE-2026-84998","CVE-2026-82171","CVE-2026-82038","CVE-2026-69155","CVE-2026-68918","CVE-2026-65963","CVE-2026-40217","CVE-2026-18079","CVE-2026-132808","CVE-2026-132807","CVE-2026-132806","CVE-2026-132805","CVE-2026-132804","CVE-2026-132803","CVE-2026-132802","CVE-2026-132627","CVE-2026-132626","CVE-2026-132625","CVE-2026-132251","CVE-2026-132250","CVE-2026-132246","CVE-2026-132237","CVE-2026-132236","CVE-20